WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.380
So, here is example number one and I posted this on my Twitter and you can see that over

00:06.380 --> 00:09.360
here we get a market structure shift, right?

00:09.360 --> 00:14.060
And then we have this autoblock, very clean autoblock, most of you would say that, okay,

00:14.060 --> 00:19.580
this is a very clean autoblock or a demand zone or whatever.

00:19.580 --> 00:24.900
But notice what happens here, price sweeps the low here, even though we had a market structure

00:24.900 --> 00:29.540
shift, we had this low as an inducement, we had this low, right?

00:29.540 --> 00:31.060
We had a fair value gap.

00:31.060 --> 00:33.820
Everything was saying, okay, go along.

00:33.820 --> 00:34.820
But what happened?

00:34.820 --> 00:39.820
Look, it just came back to the zero point, it swept the low, reclaimed, retest and it

00:39.820 --> 00:40.820
took out this high.

00:40.820 --> 00:42.420
So very, very easy trade.

